{
  "_README": [
    "Billing rates for cost estimation. EDIT THIS FILE -- nothing else needs to change.",
    "",
    "GitHub Copilot bills in AI credits. 1 AI credit = $0.01 USD.",
    "The published table quotes USD per 1,000,000 tokens; these entries are that",
    "figure x100 to express it in credits (e.g. $2.00/1M -> 200 credits/1M).",
    "",
    "Column mapping from the published table:",
    "  Input        -> credits_per_1m_input           (FRESH, uncached input only)",
    "  Cached Input -> credits_per_1m_cache_read",
    "  Cache Write  -> credits_per_1m_cache_creation  ('N/A' in the table -> null)",
    "  Output       -> credits_per_1m_output",
    "",
    "fresh = input_tokens - cache_read - cache_creation, so the three input classes",
    "are billed at their own rates and never double-counted.",
    "",
    "TIERS: models priced by context size carry a 'tiers' list, matched against the",
    "turn's input_tokens. The first tier whose max_input_tokens is >= the turn's",
    "input wins; max_input_tokens null means 'no upper bound'. A model without",
    "'tiers' uses its flat top-level fields.",
    "",
    "A null field contributes NOTHING and is not treated as zero. A model with no",
    "usable rate is reported as 'no published rate' in the UI, never as $0.00.",
    "Populate rates ONLY from the published table -- never from memory or inference."
  ],

